00:25:03.600 --> 00:25:07.680
what would you say is the most important part&nbsp;
in translating science to the wider population&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:07.680 --> 00:25:12.800
i think accuracy is obviously really important&nbsp;
but also empathy just understanding what level&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:12.800 --> 00:25:17.840
of complexity people can handle what analogies&nbsp;
would work best for explaining something and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:17.840 --> 00:25:22.640
what feels satisfying because what tends to&nbsp;
work really well for myth busting is giving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:22.640 --> 00:25:28.640
people a narrative that makes more sense than the&nbsp;
myth you have to help replace that with the truth

00:25:28.640 --> 00:25:32.480
what did you study to improve the&nbsp;
delivery of your blog posts and videos&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:32.480 --> 00:25:36.480
i think this is one of those things where the&nbsp;
best thing you can do is just practice a lot&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:36.480 --> 00:25:40.880
just make content get feedback and then&nbsp;
incorporate that into your next piece of content&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:40.880 --> 00:25:44.560
i think teaching is also really helpful because&nbsp;
it's like delivering content and getting that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:44.560 --> 00:25:48.880
real-time feedback and this doesn't have to be&nbsp;
formal teaching you could just try explaining&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:48.880 --> 00:25:52.320
the topic you're trying to make content&nbsp;
about to your friends or to your family

00:25:52.320 --> 00:25:57.680
what are the pros and cons of writing versus&nbsp;
videos so i started making videos because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:25:57.680 --> 00:26:02.560
i felt a bit constrained by blog posts some&nbsp;
things are just really hard to show you really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:02.560 --> 00:26:07.040
sort of need an animation or something moving&nbsp;
videos do take a lot longer though minus the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:07.040 --> 00:26:11.920
research a blog post would take about three&nbsp;
hours whereas a video would take 20 hours

00:26:11.920 --> 00:26:15.360
difficulties with using social media&nbsp;
i think the most annoying thing about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:15.360 --> 00:26:19.360
social media is that you have to make the&nbsp;
algorithm happy to get any sort of reach&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:19.360 --> 00:26:23.440
your posts don't get shown to your audience&nbsp;
unless you tick off a whole bunch of boxes which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:23.440 --> 00:26:27.280
change all the time and that might not be the best&nbsp;
thing for that particular piece of content maybe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:27.280 --> 00:26:32.640
you need to have a static post with lots of words&nbsp;
but the algorithm wants you to make videos social&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:32.640 --> 00:26:37.120
media is also pretty intrusive it's designed to&nbsp;
make you want to check it all the time and so&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:37.120 --> 00:26:41.840
if that's part of your work then your work-life&nbsp;
balance is a bit messed up it's particularly bad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:41.840 --> 00:26:46.720
because i'm in australia and so the peak times&nbsp;
for social media are weird hours for me things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:46.720 --> 00:26:51.920
like 2am on the other hand i do kind of like that&nbsp;
the algorithm changes all the time because i like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:26:51.920 --> 00:26:56.240
a challenge i have a short attention span&nbsp;
and so i like making lots of diverse content

00:26:56.240 --> 00:27:00.320
